###Setting up a proportion

Corresponding sides of similar triangles are proportional, so we can set up and solve a proportion:

$\dfrac{\blueE{HD}}{DG}=\dfrac{BD}{DH}$

We picked side $\blueE{\overline{HD}}$ because we need to find its length.

We picked side $\overline{DG}$ because it corresponds to side $\blueE{\overline{HD}}$.

Then we picked another pair of corresponding sides whose lengths we already knew (or which we could express in terms of $\blue{HD}$).

$\begin{array}{rcl}
&\triangle BDH
\\
{\text{hypotenuse}}
&\overbrace{\underbrace{\!\!\!\!\!\left\{ 
\dfrac{\blueE{HD}}{DG}=\dfrac{BD}{DH}
\right\}\!\!\!\!\!}}
&{\text{long} \atop \text{leg}}
\\
&\triangle HDG
\end{array}$
